# TIBIALIS RAISE

Version 1.0

---

# Purpose

The Tibialis Raise is an isolation exercise targeting the tibialis anterior to improve ankle dorsiflexion strength, lower-leg resilience and foot control.

Within CAS, it is considered a foundational robustness exercise for lower-limb durability and movement efficiency.

---

# Philosophy

A strong lower leg is not built by training the calves alone.

The tibialis anterior is essential for deceleration, foot placement and shock absorption.

CAS integrates Tibialis Raises to improve durability and support high-frequency combat movement.

